/T (Global trade grew substantially from 1990 to 2023, with volatility during crises such as 2008 and 2020. Top economies dominate imports and exports, while emerging markets are gaining significant share. Tariff policies vary widely, influencing trade costs and competitiveness. RCA and trade relations highlight competitive sectors and strong bilateral partnerships. Governments should pursue tariff harmonization and trade facilitation measures. Policymakers must support export diversification based on RCA insights. Businesses should leverage data analytics for targeted market entry and supply chain resilience. Data analytics provides critical insights into complex global trade dynamics, enabling evidence-based policy and business decisions to foster sustainable and inclusive growth.)
